use /lib/UiComponent

from /behaviors/Selection import Selection
from /behaviors/Traversal import Traversal
from /behaviors/Virtualisation import Virtualisation

export ui-component List:
    description:
        A list shows a series of items stacked one after another, each on its
        own row. The user can move through it with the keyboard and, if the
        component allows it, pick one or more items.

    behaviors:
        - @{Traversal}
        - @{Selection}
        - @{Virtualisation}

    items:
        Each item has a name that assistive tools can read out. What else an
        item shows, such as an icon or a second line of text, is up to the
        component using the list.

    picking:
        The component decides whether the list lets the user pick nothing, one
        item, or several. Clicking an item, or pressing the pick key on it,
        picks it. Which key that is is up to the chosen library.

    groups:
        Items can be put in groups under headings. Headings can't be picked,
        and the arrow keys pass over them.

    disabled:
        Disabled items are shown but can't be picked.

    empty:
        When there are no items, the component using the list decides what to
        show instead, such as "Nothing here yet".

    long:
        Virtualisation is only switched on for lists long enough to need it.

    nonGoals:
        - No items inside items. That's a tree
        - No columns. Rows of data with column headings are a table
        - No dragging to reorder
